<title>UK: UK's Clarke says BoE rate rise call &quot;wrong&quot;.</title>
<headline>UK's Clarke says BoE rate rise call &quot;wrong&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said a call by Bank of England deputy governor Howard Davies for a 0.25 percent rise in interest rates was &quot;wrong&quot;.</p>
</text>
